# DEFECT 2: 2.00 s of 16 kHz played through a 24 kHz handle finishes in 1.24 s -- 1.5x
#   fast and a fifth high. The fix reopens the device at the chunk's own rate: 1.90 s.
# DEFECT 1: the middle utterance returns in 0.00 s having played nothing, because the
#   previous write drained the buffer and ALSA failed the next one with -EPIPE.
# The NEW column's 1.90 s (not 2.00 s) is the ~100 ms ALSA ring-buffer depth: play()
#   returns when the last frames are ACCEPTED, not when the DAC has clocked them out.
#   That residual is documented on the port and in SDS 6.2.4.
